    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστεία</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰρ]</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀριστ-είη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>excellence,
				prowess,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.312
			</span></i> (Quadr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέρας ἀριστείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.36
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Gorg.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				11a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				942d
			</span></i>: <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i> are called respectively <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διομήδους,
				Ἀγαμέμνονος, Μενελάου ἀριστεία;</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				16.9
			</span></i>.</div>
